(MACHURA RAMSEY SHADOW THEORY) Tj
T*
(V04 THEORETICAL CLOSURE WITHOUT NUMERICAL PARAMETERS) Tj
T*
(====================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Author:) Tj
T*
(Michal Machura) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Scope:) Tj
T*
(This document formulates the Machura Ramsey Shadow theory without using) Tj
T*
(the numerical R\(5,5\) boundary values.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The purpose is to express the theory as a general Ramsey-theoretic) Tj
T*
(one-vertex extension and deletion calculus.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(No numerical Delta value is used in this document.) Tj
T*
(No enumeration result is used in this document.) Tj
T*
(No solver-specific mechanism is used in this document.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Standard Ramsey setting) Tj
T*
(==========================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let R\(a,b\) denote the classical Ramsey number.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A graph G is called an \(a,b\)-clean graph if:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(G contains no red K_a,) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(and the complement graph G^c contains no blue K_b.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Equivalently:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(G\) = empty,) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(where:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(G\)) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(RedK_a\(G\) union BlueK_b\(G^c\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(C_n^{a,b}) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
({G : |V\(G\)| = n and Conf_{a,b}\(G\) = empty}.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Thus C_n^{a,b} is the layer of clean Ramsey cores on n vertices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. One-vertex extension) Tj
T*
(=======================) Tj
T*
ET
