() Tj
T*
(Let G be a graph on vertex set V.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let chi be a connection map from a new vertex to the old core:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(chi : V\(G\) -> {red, blue}.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The extended graph is denoted:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(G + chi.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The shadow Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\) is defined as the set of all new forbidden) Tj
T*
(Ramsey conflicts created with the participation of the added vertex.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Thus Phi contains exactly those forbidden structures which did not exist) Tj
T*
(inside G alone and which become complete after adding the new vertex.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Forward shadow identity) Tj
T*
(==========================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For every graph G and every connection map chi:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(G + chi\)) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(G\) union Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In score form:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(score_{a,b}\(G + chi\)) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(score_{a,b}\(G\) + |Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\)|.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If G is clean, then:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(G\) = empty,) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(so:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(G + chi\)) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Therefore, for a clean core, the whole obstruction to a clean extension) Tj
T*
(is exactly the shadow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Reverse shadow identity) Tj
T*
(==========================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let H be a graph and let v be a vertex of H.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Define:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(G_v = H - v.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Let chi_v be the connection map induced by the deleted vertex v:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(chi_v : V\(G_v\) -> {red, blue}.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
