(Then:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(H\)) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(Conf_{a,b}\(H - v\) union Phi_{a,b,H-v}\(chi_v\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In score form:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(score_{a,b}\(H\)) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(score_{a,b}\(H - v\) + |Phi_{a,b,H-v}\(chi_v\)|.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Equivalently:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(|Phi_{a,b,H-v}\(chi_v\)|) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(score_{a,b}\(H\) - score_{a,b}\(H - v\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Interpretation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The shadow of a deleted vertex is exactly the part of the Ramsey conflict) Tj
T*
(score that disappears when the vertex is removed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Vertex-sum identity) Tj
T*
(======================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Summing the reverse shadow over all vertices of H gives:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(sum_{v in V\(H\)} |Phi_v\(H\)|) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(a * |RedK_a\(H\)| + b * |BlueK_b\(H^c\)|.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Reason:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every red K_a has exactly a vertices, so it is counted once for each) Tj
T*
(of its vertices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every blue K_b has exactly b vertices, so it is counted once for each) Tj
T*
(of its vertices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This gives a global consistency check for the shadow calculus.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Shadow reversal lemma) Tj
T*
(========================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The following statements are equivalent:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A. There exists a clean graph H on succ\(n\) vertices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(B. There exists a clean core G in C_n^{a,b} and a connection map chi) Tj
T*
(   such that:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\) = empty.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Proof from B to A:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If G is clean and Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\) is empty, then:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
