(==========================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(To refute shadow closure at a given layer, it is enough to find one pair:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(\(G, chi\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(such that:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(G in C_n^{a,b},) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(and:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\) = empty.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Such a pair immediately constructs a clean graph:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(H = G + chi) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(on succ\(n\) vertices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Thus the entire closure claim is falsified by one empty shadow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(9. Quantitative Delta layer) Tj
T*
(===========================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The qualitative theory requires only:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\) is not empty.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The quantitative version defines:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Delta_{a,b}\(n -> succ\(n\)\)) Tj
T*
(=) Tj
T*
(min_{G in C_n^{a,b}} min_chi |Phi_{a,b,G}\(chi\)|.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Then:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Delta_{a,b}\(n -> succ\(n\)\) > 0) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(is equivalent to shadow closure at that layer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A concrete numerical value of Delta belongs to the evidence and audit) Tj
T*
(layer, not to the abstract theory in this document.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(10. Relation to validated tests) Tj
T*
(===============================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The forward and reverse identities were locally validated on real clean) Tj
T*
(Ramsey cores by the following tests:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(V01:) Tj
T*
(Shadow reversal validation.) Tj
T*
(Clean H gives clean deleted cores and empty reconstructed shadow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(V03:) Tj
T*
(Shadow difference validation.) Tj
T*
(The deleted-vertex shadow equals score\(H\) - score\(H-v\), including) Tj
T*
(separate red and blue components and the vertex-sum identity.) Tj
